<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austrian Littoral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1849–1918</span> · Also known as Küstenland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Austrian Littoral was a crown land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> on the northern Adriatic, formed in 1849 from the coastal parts of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyria">Illyria</a>. It comprised the free city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a>, the Margraviate of Istria and the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorizia">Gorizia</a> and Gradisca, governed from Trieste. Its mixed Italian, Slovene and Croatian population made it a contested region, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> annexed most of it after 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austrian-littoral.jpg" alt="Austrian Littoral" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Austrian_Littoral_with_coat_of_arms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
